A continuous random variable $X$ has $P(X < 6) = 0.24$ and $P(X < 13) = 0.79$. Find $P(6 \le X \le 13)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.29cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=6:13, variable=\x] (6,0) -- plot ({\x},{2.2*exp(-0.5*((\x-10)/3.5)*((\x-10)/3.5))}) -- (13,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (21.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5) -- (0,2.9) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick, domain=0:20, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2.2*exp(-0.5*((\x-10)/3.5)*((\x-10)/3.5))});
\draw (6,0) -- (6,1.145);
\draw (13,0) -- (13,1.524);
\node[below] at (6,0) {$6$};
\node[below] at (13,0) {$13$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A continuous random variable $X$ has $P(2 \le X \le 7) = 0.58$. Which statement is correct?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.6cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=2:7, variable=\x] (2,0) -- plot ({\x},{2.2*exp(-0.5*((\x-4.5)/2)*((\x-4.5)/2))}) -- (7,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (10.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.5) -- (0,2.9) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick, domain=0:9.5, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2.2*exp(-0.5*((\x-4.5)/2)*((\x-4.5)/2))});
\draw (2,0) -- (2,1.007);
\draw (7,0) -- (7,1.007);
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node[below] at (7,0) {$7$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
